{
  "title": "Deep copy and copy-and-swap: Tableau v3/v4",
  "chapter": "04-classes",
  "summary": "Slides 107 and 111: a copy constructor that duplicates the buffer, and an assignment that copies into a temporary and swaps.",
  "code": "Tableau( const Tableau & t )\n  : taille_{ t.taille_ }, tab_{ new double[t.taille_] } { /* copy elements */ }\n\nTableau & operator=( const Tableau & t ) {\n  Tableau tmp{ t };     // 1. copy\n  swap( tmp );          // 2. exchange representations\n  return *this;\n}                       // 3. tmp dies with our OLD buffer\n\nint main() {\n  Tableau a{ 2 };\n  Tableau b{ a };       // deep copy\n  Tableau c{ 3 };\n  c = a;                // copy-and-swap\n}",
